# Agent scratch, written by tooling rather than by hand. Untracked, so CI never
# sees it -- but `format:check` walks the whole tree, so a single session note
# halts the first step of `npm run verify` and takes the rest of the chain with
# it. Two agents hit that separately on 2026-08-15 and each worked around it,
# which is how the frontend chain went a whole session without being run end to
# end. Ignoring the path is cheaper than rewriting files nobody authored.
.claude/tackline

# Real authored lesson files, lifted verbatim out of the event log for
# `slides.test.ts` to segment. Formatting them defeats the point of checking
# them in: the segmentation rule is fitted to the shape a `lesson-drafter`
# actually writes, and a prettier pass rewraps prose and normalises emphasis --
# so the fixture becomes a document nobody authored, which is the failure
# CLAUDE.md's "checkpoints over model output" section is about.
src/domain/lesson/fixtures
